// What a client may ask about a file of the vault as it opens it.
//
// A file is the person's own bytes: a scanned book, a recording, a picture.
// What is here is what a viewer has to know before it can draw one — how many
// pages, how long it runs, where a passage sits on the page — and never the
// bytes themselves. Those are answered at addresses of their own, because a
// browser's own elements speak bytes and not this.
//
